>> 1) What artifacts do you have?  How many have been created so far?
>+1 Stormbringer, +7 Bat, Eyes of the Overworld, GoD...
Well, you have great melee and defense, but you would have to waste a
lot of of wishes to get any more artifacts.  It might be worth it if
you convert to neutral, and then wish for the Eye of the Aethiopica.
With Pw regen, crystal golems are truly superior.  You would have to
buy back all of your protection, but you should be able to afford it.

> Haven't been past 28 yet, though (where the Adventurers are still
> waiting for young Bob #7 so they can mess him up like they did his
> cousin, Bob #4)

See my advice about clearing this level with the help of pet basilisks,
a scroll of earth, and a ring of protection from shape changers.  You
may have to remove the Eyes when you are surrounded by boulders, so
that the Adventurers don't fire wands at you.

>> 4) What spells do you know?
>ID, Charm Monster, Magic Missile, Sleep, Dig, Finger of Death (100%),
>Force Bolt. Jesus, about 20 others. The only ones that I'm using are
>Charm and ID.
You should also be using "Haste self" and jumping.  Just because you
like water walking is no excuse not to be "very fast" .

By the way, an interesting pet to have is a rhaumbusun, especially
combined with other pets.  Its gaze attack is quite amusing.  It will
probably annoy shopkeepers, though.

>> 5) What are your unpolymorphed stats?
>St 18/20, Dx:23, Co:20, In:25, Wi:25, Ch:15, HP:124, Pw:199, AC:-39, Exp:16

Excellent.  HP should be higher, but you will have tons of full healing
potions after you finish clearing the DA level and an alchemy session.
You will probably also want to get up to level 20 so you can use the
power surge technique.

>> 9) Do you have any high-rate firearms and ammo?
>Assault rifle. Currently visiting Ludios with my pet purple worm,
>Jackson Pollock, but unfortunately the soldiers were too fast with the
>grenades and hardly any bullets survived... :-(

Hmm.  Sounds like you need a lesson in bullet conservation.
- Soldiers will not throw grenades if they can't see/sense you
Purple worm or basilisk pets are ideal for killing all the soldiers,
but you need to make sure that they don't throw the grenades.  Usually
I use a wand of teleport to send my hasted purple worm into the main
Ludios chamber, and then just wait with a blindfold until all the
soldiers disappear, before I even look for the secret door.

>> 8) What techniques can you perform?
> t---- (Slashem geekcode for: techniques? wazzat? :-) )

Liquid Leap is very useful.  Disarm can be very useful.  Draw energy
and Power surge can also help - and these are just the defensive techs.

Remember, you are NOT immortal.  Getting intrinsic magical breathing
and wearing lifesaving instead of unchanging will protect you from
almost all YASD's.

Try not to get too bored.

Happy Hacking.



